**Section 21 directions** (public interest, depositors' interest or **banking policy**) may fix:

- the **purpose** for which advances may or may not be made;
- **margins** on secured advances;
- the **maximum advance** to any borrower, in relation to **paid-up capital, reserves and deposits**;
- the **maximum guarantees**;
- **interest rates and other terms**.

**Selective credit control** prevents **speculative hoarding** of essential goods (food grains, pulses, oilseeds, sugar, cotton and textiles) by limiting **credit and its price**; it is little used now.

**Section 20 restrictions:** no loan on the **security of the bank's own shares**; no loan or commitment to **a director**, or to a **firm in which a director is partner, manager, employee or guarantor**, or a **company in which a director holds substantial interest or is a director**, except a **Section 25 (Section 8) company**; and no loan to a person whose **guarantor or partner is a director**. In case of **doubt** whether a transaction is a loan, the **Reserve Bank decides**.

**Section 20A:** **no remission of a debt of a director or of a related firm** without **prior Reserve Bank permission**; remission in breach is **void**.
